  "ruleKubbFieldTitle": "The field",
  "ruleKubbFieldBody": "Two teams face each other across the field. Each lines up five kubbs on its baseline, and the king stands alone in the middle.",
  "ruleKubbFieldDetail": "Tournament fields measure 5 × 8 meters. In the park, two jackets and a good guess work fine — just keep the halves roughly equal.",
  "ruleKubbTeamsTitle": "One to six per team",
  "ruleKubbTeamsBody": "Kubb is a team game: one to six players per team. Teammates share the six batons and take turns throwing.",
  "ruleKubbBatonsTitle": "Six batons per turn",
  "ruleKubbBatonsBody": "The attacking team throws six batons at the other team's kubbs — underhand, spinning end over end.",
  "ruleKubbBatonsDetail": "No helicopter throws: the baton must spin vertically, never sideways. Kubbs felled by the batons stay down until the turn ends.",
  "ruleKubbThrowInTitle": "Felled kubbs come back",
  "ruleKubbThrowInBody": "After the batons, the defenders throw every felled kubb into the attackers' half. Where a kubb lands, it is stood up as a field kubb.",
  "ruleKubbThrowInDetail": "The defenders choose where to aim — kubbs standing close together are far easier to clear with one baton.",
  "ruleKubbFieldFirstTitle": "Field kubbs first",
  "ruleKubbFieldFirstBody": "Attackers must fell every standing field kubb before any baseline kubb may be hit. A baseline kubb felled too early is raised again.",
  "ruleKubbPenaltyTitle": "Out twice = penalty",
  "ruleKubbPenaltyBody": "A kubb thrown out of bounds twice becomes a penalty kubb: the other team places it anywhere in their half — even right next to the king.",
  "ruleKubbAdvantageTitle": "The advantage line",
  "ruleKubbAdvantageBody": "If your opponents leave field kubbs standing in your half, your team may throw its batons from level with the one closest to the king.",
  "ruleKubbKingTitle": "The king decides it",
  "ruleKubbKingBody": "Only when every kubb in the defending half is down may you aim for the king. Topple it, and the game is yours.",
  "ruleKubbEarlyKingTitle": "Not before the line is down",
  "ruleKubbEarlyKingBody": "Topple the king before everything else is down — even by accident — and your team loses the game on the spot.",
  "ruleKubbMatchTitle": "Best of three",
  "ruleKubbMatchBody": "Tournaments play a match as best of three games. The teams alternate which team opens each game.",
  "ruleKubbMatchDetail": "With the turn clock on, a team has a fixed time to throw its six batons. The clock is a guide — the app never blocks a throw.",
